      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "NIU Shu-yü 鈕樹玉 (T. 藍田, 匪[非]石, 1760–1827), Nov. 5, scholar, was a native of Tung-t'ing shan 洞庭山, southwest of Soochow. He lost his parents in childhood and made his living by peddling cotton goods; but having set his heart early on learning, he studied the classics in leisure hours.",
          "source": "eccp-3649162",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        },
